    [
     1,
     "<div>Hello,</div><div>I&#39;m only OK with using dartR but since no one answered - and in case you still need help I&#39;ll try.</div><div><br></div><br><div>When I run structure there are no + symbols in my commands.  I use a rstudio on mac.</div><div><br></div><div>Example command that works or me - this was a small test run to see if my I could get output for mapping and such:</div><div><br></div><div>structure &lt;- gl.run.structure(result,<br>                              exec = &quot;./structure&quot;,<br>                              noadmix = FALSE,<br>                              k.range = 2:4,<br>                              num.k.rep = 2,<br>                              burnin = 10,<br>                              numreps = 100,<br>                              inferalpha = TRUE,<br>                              delete.files = FALSE)</div><div><br></div><div>Since larger data and lots of reps takes a LONG time to run, I would suggest you make a smaller version of your dataset to run. Even if you get it running the output may not be as you wish (I had my lat lon incorrectly formatted for example).</div><div><br></div><div>Finally, my last suggestion would be to try to put Structure app directly in your folder.  I never could get it to run correctly when using a path (even though I use paths all the time for other things in rstudio).  I also needed plink in the folder, it was available in the original folder I downloaded with the structure app.  I found that out by reading the Pritchard site for the Structure app.</div><div><br></div><div>Good luck!</div>"
    ],
